    "title": "Western Kentucky Farmers Fight Natural Gas Pipeline - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thunderbolt Newsroom ,\n1 days ago Farmers in western Kentucky are pushing back against a proposed 53-mile natural gas pipeline that would cross private property. Channel 6 reports Caldwell County farmer Firmon Cook says construction could damage his farmland, including soil and drainage systems. He also calls the company’s initial offer of $4 per foot for access to his land too low. Read full article\n17",
